ce of  the oncoming myeloid assay  which is able to evaluate  all 40 genes that are highly represented  in  myeloid neoplasms that i discussed as  well as  identify 29 fusion driver genes  as well as over 600 fusion isotypes  the advantage of this system is  that it's able to analyze all of these  genetic alterations that are highly  enriched in  myeloproliferative neoplasms  myelodysplastic syndromes  mds npn as well as the acute myeloid  leukemias  using relatively low sample input at  about 20 nanograms  of dna and rna this is a dna  rna-based panel testing it  is a single platform and the results are  provided within 24  to 48 hours  our preliminary data indicates  that this platform could be highly  suitable  for two applications one to be able  to function as a initial molecular  screening assay for us to be able to  triage bone marrows based on flow  cytometry  and the rapid ngf panel  to be able to allocate  the specimen into these four large  the second large application would be in  the diagnostic workup  of acute myeloid leukemias to be able to  identify  both the dna based mutations as well as  the  fusion genes that would be critical  for identifying genetic alterations that  contribute to diagnosis  as well as identify actionable genetic  alterations  within a 24-hour time frame  as well as provide information about  risk  stratification  to summarize we believe that  recent advances in the ngs technology  for oncology research  are providing great promise for future  precision oncology testing  and one example is the oncoming myeloda  gx  on the iron torn genexis system which  enables  robust variant detection and  represents an easy to use workflow  that results or provide results in  as short of a time frame as a single day  and these advancements could represent  future opportunities for  implementing ngs as a first-line  strategy for  triaging suspected myeloid malignancies  thank you and i would be happy to take  questions  and thank you very muc